  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Erythronium dens-canis",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythronium_dens-canis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1355297564,
      "text": "Erythronium dens-canis, the dog's-tooth-violet is a bulbous herbaceous perennial flowering plant in the family Liliaceae. It is native to central and southern Europe from Portugal to Ukraine, and locally naturalised north to Germany, Great Britain, and Ireland. It, and the closely related Erythronium caucasicum in the extreme southeast of Europe, are the only naturally occurring species of Erythronium in Europe. Despite its common name, it is not closely related to the true violets of genus Viola."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Erythronium dens-canis",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythronium_dens-canis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 168829018,
      "text": "Erythronium dens-canis, comúnmente conocida como diente de perro, diente sangriento o mantecón, es la única especie del género Erythronium nativa de Europa, donde crece en forma silvestre. Se puede encontrar en España, por ejemplo en el Torcal de Antequera."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Dent de chien",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dent_de_chien",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 219439550,
      "text": "La Dent-de-chien est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Liliaceae. C'est une plante herbacée à bulbe vivace originaire des montagnes européennes et d'Asie."
    }
  },
